  "rationale": "The question asks for biochemical inhibition of Q04771 (ACVR1/ALK2), so a purified-kinase assay is the correct system; cell viability cards (cell-prepare/cell-expose/cell-detect) are excluded because they measure cellular ATP/viability, not target-specific inhibition. Retained ChEMBL examples (CHEMBL3365510, CHEMBL4815728, CHEMBL3789973, CHEMBL2390524) confirm that ACVR1/ALK2 inhibition is routinely measured biochemically with kinase plus substrate plus ATP, with 30-45 min incubations; however, all retained examples are radiometric filter-binding assays, not ADP-Glo, so the ADP-Glo readout is an adaptation chosen for safety and throughput, and its compatibility with ACVR1 is an assumption. The concentration series, replicates, and DMSO fraction are design assumptions, not sourced facts, since the packet contains no measurement for CHEMBL1078178 and no retrieved example is similarity-ranked to it.",
